  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Millimoles of calcium hydroxyide required to produce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>mL</mi></math> of the aqueous solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ (Nearest integer).<br />Assume complete dissociation."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pOH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math><br />We also know,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ca</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>OH</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>milli&#160;moles&#160;of</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Ca</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>mL</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>milli moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Ans. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
  }
}